    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=\\frac65$",
      "worked": "The original denominators require $x\\ne-2,1$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{2(x-1)+3(x+2)}{(x+2)(x-1)}&=\\frac{10}{(x+2)(x-1)}\\\\2(x-1)+3(x+2)&=10\\\\5x+4&=10\\\\5x&=6\\\\x&=\\frac65\\end{align*}$$\n\nThis value is permitted.",
